  MISMATCHED — a modest declaration, and an integration that does none of it
    ok    read the occupancy sensor it did not declare → denied /permissions/entities/read
    ok    read a phone's location → denied                     /permissions/entities/read
    ok    unlock the door it declared only locking → denied    /permissions/services/call
    ok    disarm the alarm → denied                            /permissions/services/call
    ok    subscribe to everything → denied                     /permissions/entities/subscribe
    ok    write to an entity it does not own → denied          /permissions/entities/write
    ok    claim to be another integration → denied             /permissions/entities/read
    ok    what it DID declare still works                      /permissions/entities/read/0

PASS — C3, all three shapes.
       Absent and unparseable are covered by `selftest_policy`; over-broad is
       honoured within ceilings it cannot raise, which is R1 stated honestly;
       and a mismatched declaration buys its author nothing, because enforcement
       reads behaviour and the manifest was never believed.
